/target
# Each crate under crates/unsafe/ is its own workspace with its own build.
crates/unsafe/*/target
# A cargo run from inside a crate's directory builds there; 0.0.200 committed
# one such tree by accident (crates/nikaia/target/floor), removed in 0.0.227.
crates/*/target
/vendor

# Dependencies of the TextMate grammar's scope test (editors/test). The lockfile
# beside it is committed: it pins the version of the reference implementation the
# test's result means anything against.
node_modules/

# Subagent git worktrees (created by the agent harness, never part of the project).
.claude/worktrees/

# Stray build artifacts that were committed once at the repository root.
/hello_world
/hello_world.rs
/check_rustc.rs

# A stray rustc invocation without `-o` leaves one of these.
/a.out

# What `nikaia --input examples/x.nika` leaves beside the source it lowered: the
# Rust, and the ledger of the one file it was pointed at. A project build writes
# both into its own output directory, and a package's real ledger is committed
# ([ADR-020](docs/specification/adr/adr-020.md)) - so these are listed by the
# three directories where a bare `--input` is run by hand, and nowhere wider.
# The committed Rust under `benches/*/src/` is not matched: a generated file
# lands *beside* the `.nika` it came from, never in a `src/`.
/examples/*.rs
/examples/nikaia.contracts
/examples/nikaia.derived
# What `nikaia test` or `nikaia run` leaves inside an example package: the build
# of a run in place, which is how `tests/examples.rs` runs them (#534): its
# builds are reused from one run to the next. Its `nikaia.lock` and ledgers are
# committed and checked by `scripts/ledgers.nika` (#2797).
/examples/*/target/
# The yaml bench's programs check in a package each (#1974); a check or a run
# in place leaves its build and lockfile there. `bench.nika` builds each from
# a copy with a manifest of its own, never in place, so no build checks this
# lock (#2797).
/benches/yaml/*/target/
/benches/yaml/*/nikaia.lock
/benches/*.rs
/benches/nikaia.contracts
/benches/nikaia.derived
/tests/samples/*.rs
/tests/samples/nikaia.contracts
/tests/samples/nikaia.derived
# And in `std`'s own directory of the toolchain's Nikaia, where a module is
# lowered by hand while it is written; `nikaia lower-std` writes the `.rs` that
# is committed, and nothing reads a ledger here (0.0.253 removed the one that
# had been committed by accident at 0.0.169).
/crates/nikaia-std/src/compiler/nikaia.contracts
/crates/nikaia-std/src/compiler/nikaia.derived
# The toolchain's own packages (`within = "std"`, #1976) are lowered by
# `nikaia lower-std`, never built in place, so no build checks a lock or a
# ledger of theirs: what a `nikaia build` or `check` run there by hand leaves
# is not a record of anything (#2797).
/crates/nikaia-std/src/compiler/nikaia.lock
/crates/nikaia-std/src/runtime/nikaia.lock
/crates/nikaia-std/src/runtime/nikaia.contracts
/crates/nikaia-std/src/runtime/nikaia.derived

# The documentation site, as `scripts/site-build.sh` builds it, and what the
# build and `wrangler` leave beside it.
/website/_site/
/website/.wrangler/
/_site/
/.jekyll-cache/
/.sass-cache/
/.wrangler/
/scripts/site-jekyll/Gemfile.lock

# The test packages build in place, so a test run of one reuses its build;
# their `nikaia.lock` and ledgers are committed like every in-place project's
# and checked by CI (#2797).
/tests/language/target
/tests/build-time/target
/tests/compiler/target

# A package built in place keeps its build tree beside it.
packages/*/target

# Session state of the main-session scripts (agent.nika, cycle.nika, drive.nika)
docs/briefs/**/RED
docs/briefs/**/ESCALATE
docs/briefs/**/QUESTION
docs/briefs/**/STOP
docs/briefs/**/architect-input.txt
docs/briefs/**/*.session
docs/briefs/**/qa-input.txt
docs/briefs/**/suite.log
docs/briefs/**/unpushed.txt

# Briefs, reports and a run's numbers live beside the tree and on the issue
# (#1252): a commit of them would start a CI run that tests nothing.
/docs/briefs/

# Python bytecode the scripts leave beside themselves (#1659).
__pycache__/
